      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:101:4",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ مَا يَنْبَغِي لِلْمُؤْمِنِ أَنْ يَسْتَوْحِشَ إِلَى أَخِيهِ فَمَنْ دُونَهُ الْمُؤْمِنُ عَزِيزٌ فِي دِينِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from Muhammad Bin Isa, from Yunus, from Kuleyb Bin Muawiya, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I heard him<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘It is not befitting for the <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span> that he alienates to his brother from the ones below him (in understanding). The <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span>een are highly valued people in their Religion’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Yunus from Kulayb ibn Mu’awiyah who has said the following: “I heard abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) saying, ‘It does not benefit a believer to be apprehensive of his brother (in belief) of less perfect belief; believers are highly valued people in their religion.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
